#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184011 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02f49ab2-8f14-568c-a602-abd2ed979ff7" :knowledge-point/title "Expanding a Binomial"}] :question/id #uuid "a4f624b3-da2f-5b89-affb-374bcf2f5a75" :question/math-academy-id "e-5155" :question/problem "Find the first $3$ terms in ascending powers of $a$ of the binomial expansion of $(1+3a)^5$." :question/worked-solution "The first $3$ terms of the binomial expansion for ${(1 + x)^n}$ are given by\n\n$$\n{(1 + x)^n} = 1 + nx + \\frac{{n(n - 1)}}{{2!}}{x^2} + \\cdots\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=3a$ and $n=5$ into the above formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(1 + 3a)^{5} &= 1 + 5(3a) + (5(5 - 1))/(2!)(3a)^{2} + ⋯ \\\\\n&= 1 + 5(3a) + (5(4))/(2)(9a^{2}) + ⋯ \\\\\n&= 1 + 15a + 90a^{2} + ⋯\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184047 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df318a39-103a-53a6-99f8-2ccf3601f3ca" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Coefficient of a Binomial Expansion"}] :question/id #uuid "0094b7a6-a55e-57aa-9ee0-7c5fcd803c82" :question/math-academy-id "e-9778" :question/problem "Determine the coefficient of $r^3$ in the expansion of $\\left(1 - 3r \\right)^{10}$." :question/worked-solution "The binomial expansion for $(1 + x)^n$ is given by\n\n$$\n(1 + x)^n = 1 + nx + \\frac{n(n - 1)}{2!} x^2 + \\cdots\n$$\n\nIn particular, the $x^3$ term is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{n(n-1)(n-2)}{3!} x^3\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-3r$ and $n$ with $10$ in the above expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(10(10 - 1)(10 - 2))/(3!)(-3r)^{3} &= (10(9)(8))/(6) \\cdot (-3)^{3} \\cdot r^{3} \\\\\n&= (10(9)(8))/(6) \\cdot (-27)r^{3} \\\\\n&=-3240r^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of $r^3$ is $-3\\,240$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184048 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f3ba60a-8c09-563f-ae02-8183bb55e359" :knowledge-point/title "Expanding a Binomial With Negative Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "ca98d9bd-337e-5982-9609-e3d0f4601575" :question/math-academy-id "e-9779" :question/problem "Find the first $3$ terms in ascending powers of $m$ of the binomial expansion of $\\left(1 - \\dfrac{4m}{3}\\right)^7$." :question/worked-solution "The first $3$ terms of the binomial expansion for ${(1 + x)^n}$ are given by\n\n$$\n{(1 + x)}^n = 1 + nx + \\frac{{n(n - 1)}}{{2!}}{x^2} + \\cdots\n$$\n\nBy substituting\n\n$$\nx=-\\dfrac{4m}{3}\n$$\n\nand $n=7$ into the above formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(1 - \\frac{4m}{3})^{7} &= 1 + 7(-\\frac{4m}{3}) + (7(7 - 1))/(2!)(-\\frac{4m}{3})^{2} + ⋯ \\\\\n&= 1 + 7(-\\frac{4m}{3}) + (7(6))/(2)(-\\frac{4m}{3})^{2} + ⋯ \\\\\n&= 1 + 7(-\\frac{4m}{3}) + (7(6))/(2)(\\frac{16m^{2}}{9}) + ⋯ \\\\\n&= 1 - \\frac{28m}{3} + \\frac{112m^{2}}{3} + ⋯\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184404 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02f49ab2-8f14-568c-a602-abd2ed979ff7" :knowledge-point/title "Expanding a Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b343456c-53fd-5137-9b29-b5eebc08903f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + 42t + 360t^{2} + ⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186180874} {:answer/id #uuid "f688c68f-c857-5ded-a9ae-ba16d1a7472e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + 42t + 728t^{2} + ⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186180875} {:answer/id #uuid "188ddf88-762f-5e11-9652-a7607b831ed8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + 42t + 724t^{2} + ⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186180876} {:answer/id #uuid "222d32e7-a19c-5799-aa79-f281320d4313" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + 42t + 756t^{2} + ⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186180877} {:answer/id #uuid "3a6b1666-323f-5575-8f64-05cd89c4ac1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + 42t + 740t^{2} + ⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186180878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "222d32e7-a19c-5799-aa79-f281320d4313" :answer/ty